<title>JAPAN: Thai govt to refrain from buying rubber-minister.</title>
<headline>Thai govt to refrain from buying rubber-minister.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai government will refrain from buying rubber for a while as domestic prices are above the minimum price of 27.5 baht per kg, Deputy Agriculture Minister Grich Gongpechara said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not going to buy rubber, considering current rubber prices in Thailand,&quot; the minister told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>A senior agriculture ministry official said late in March that the Thai government had bought 26,400 tonnes of rubber since March 5 to support domestic rubber prices and intended to buy more rubber in the future.</p>
<p>The Thai government guarantees a minimum price for local rubber at 27.5 baht per kg.</p>
<p>The deputy agriculture minister is currently in Japan for meetings with industry officials.</p>
</text>
